{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and a 12th-century Crusader leader. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Born around 1134 he was the heir to the County of Tripoli. In 1152 he succeeded his father as the Count of Tripoli.\n\n* **Early Life and Accession** *\nRaymond III was known for his military prowess and leadership skills. He took part in the Second Crusade and fought against the Muslim forces in the region. He also played a key role in the Battle of Harenc in 1163 where he defeated the forces of Nur ad-Din.\n\nIn 1163 he married Eschiva of Beirut daughter of Amalric I of Jerusalem and his wife Agnes of Courtenay. The marriage was a strategic one as it strengthened the ties between the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. * **Marriage and Children** *\n\nThe marriage between Raymond III and Eschiva produced three children including a daughter who would go on to marry Bohemond III of Antioch. Raymond III also had a son named Bohemond who would go on to become the Count of Tripoli. \n\n* **Death and Succession** *\nRaymond III died in 1187 after being captured by Saladin during the Battle of Hattin. He was later executed in the city of Tripoli. He was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV who went on to become a prominent leader in the region.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.3748852e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0082991